    "reaction": "I am stopping in the night of 19 July, rain due tomorrow, with about 55 cut and 310 standing. Choosing I am confused put the words I am confused into the note box by itself; I did not type it and I am not submitting. I liked the sums and the people with reasons: Zehra asking who will feed her family, Maryam changing her excuse to talk at the spring, Yusuf saying his wife is in the field. But I could not tell what time was doing: an afternoon that lasted ten minutes, a Skip that went grey and changed nothing I could see, a ledger whose abouts add up differently each time, a hold that worked at one length and not the next, and once the reply list printed one letter per line. I would leave it paused overnight, not running. I might come back another evening to see whether the rain came and what the field count says, if I could be told plainly when time is moving.",
